💡 **SUGGESTION: make the bootstrap-skip contract local to `runPublishCommands`**

`runPublishCommands` skips dedup on **position**: `commands.slice(1)` silently assumes `commands[0]` is always the branch bootstrap. That invariant is only documented 60 lines away, in `publishCommands`' doc comment ("First command bootstraps the data branch…"). If `publishCommands` ever gains a leading command or reorders, the dedup would skip the wrong command every publish — silent board staleness, hard to diagnose from the tick log.

Two cheap ways to make the contract local:

```javascript
// option A — skip by shape, not position
var bootstrapAt = commands.reduce(function (at, c, i) {
    return at === -1 && c.indexOf('gh api -X POST ') === 0 ? i : at;
}, -1);
var rest = bootstrapped ? commands.filter(function (c, i) { return i !== bootstrapAt; })
                        : commands;
```

```javascript
// option B — state the coupling in the doc block
/** @param commands publishCommands() output — commands[0] MUST be the
 *  branch bootstrap (this is the command the bootKey probe skips). */
```

Behavior today is correct (AC2 pins it), so this is polish-tier: either option is fine, or close the thread as wontfix.

